# Project instructions — {{project_name}}

Read Proposal.md first. Work only within its accepted scope and current user
authorization. Do not invent requirements, facts, source credits or test results.

- For projects, use a local Git clone plus an approved private GitHub repository.
  Do not create repositories for everyday tasks or simple chats.
- Keep secrets, personal settings, private notes and personal paths out of Git.
  Use ignored local-only/ and demo examples. Public attribution must be approved.
- Keep documentation concise and factual. No filler, unsupported marketing,
  fabricated benchmarks, repetitive boilerplate comments or false validation claims.
- Keep README, LICENSE, .gitignore, source credits and the dated change log current.
- Use coherent commits and reviewed feature branches. Preserve history and tags.
  Never force-push main. Public publication and paid calls require authorization.
- Default language: en-US. Maintain pt-BR, es-AR, es-MX, es-ES, de-DE and fr-FR docs.
- Each new file needs a clear role, data classification, actual source/attribution
  when relevant, and validation appropriate to its behavior. Use the file templates;
  do not add ceremonial comments that merely repeat the implementation.
- Report actual checks, unresolved issues and remaining limits before handoff.
